    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d539">

                <pb facs="0762" n="660" xml:id="pg660"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/1442: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gilbert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-09-28T10:00:00+01:00">September 28,
                            1935—10 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 28—8:15 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>389. Consulate’s 386, September 27, 5 p.m.<anchor n="85" xml:id="d539-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>2. The following telegram was sent last night by the Secretary General to the
                    Emperor of Ethiopia.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“Committee of the Council has taken note of Your Majesty’s decision to
                        withdraw Ethiopian troops to 30 kilometres from the frontier and appreciates
                        the spirit in which this decision has been taken. The Committee, considering
                        with the most careful attention your request for despatch of impartial
                        observers, is examining whether the actual circumstances would permit them
                        to discharge their mission.”</p>
                </quote>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gilbert</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d539-f1" n="85" xml:id="d539-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; but see Consulate’s telegram No. 376, September 26, 10 a.m., <ref
                        target="#pg658">p. 658</ref>.</p>
            </note>
